{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages","id":1515669,"title":"Making life challenging for Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-20T08:22:28-07:00","id":1515669,"title":"Making life challenging for Mages","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I normally hang around the Werewolf Forms, but I have a keen interest in all the Chronicles of Darkness games. I wanted to ask how to make life\u2026challenging\u2026 for Mages. I get that Mages are arguably the most powerful entities in the Chronicles of Darkness, but I imagine that they must have some weaknesses. I am sorry if this thread was done to death in the past but I am curious</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1/ Mages are Squishy: The most obvious point is that Mages are just ordinary people when you look at it and break easy. Sure they can get Mage armor, but some of the mage armors are tougher than others and using Mana to heal is very inefficient compared to other splats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2/ Mages need to prepare: Mages are virtual demigods when they have time to prepare with rituals, but when caught unprepared they are vulnerable</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3/ Mages have blind spots: My impression is that Mages can usually do some things really well, but are not that useful in others. For instance, a Mage with a high value in the Death Arcana would be great against Ghosts, but pretty hopeless when faced with a Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4/ Mages need Mana: My impression is that Mana is mainly used to prevent paradox due to reach (correct me if I am wrong), and that Mages can burn through it quickly through spell casting. They also need it for Healing (however limited). However, if they burn through their Mana reserves they are forced to confront Paradox which might blow up in their faces, or scourge their bodies which is very unhealthy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know if I am missing anything. </span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T08:52:43-07:00","id":1515671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I normally hang around the Werewolf Forms, but I have a keen interest in all the Chronicles of Darkness games. I wanted to ask how to make life\u2026challenging\u2026 for Mages. I get that Mages are arguably the most powerful entities in the Chronicles of Darkness, but I imagine that they must have some weaknesses. I am sorry if this thread was done to death in the past but I am curious</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1/ Mages are Squishy: The most obvious point is that Mages are just ordinary people when you look at it and break easy. Sure they can get Mage armor, but some of the mage armors are tougher than others and using Mana to heal is very inefficient compared to other splats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2/ Mages need to prepare: Mages are virtual demigods when they have time to prepare with rituals, but when caught unprepared they are vulnerable</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3/ Mages have blind spots: My impression is that Mages can usually do some things really well, but are not that useful in others. For instance, a Mage with a high value in the Death Arcana would be great against Ghosts, but pretty hopeless when faced with a Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4/ Mages need Mana: My impression is that Mana is mainly used to prevent paradox due to reach (correct me if I am wrong), and that Mages can burn through it quickly through spell casting. They also need it for Healing (however limited). However, if they burn through their Mana reserves they are forced to confront Paradox which might blow up in their faces, or scourge their bodies which is very unhealthy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know if I am missing anything. </span></span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Any good mage is certain to make their own life difficult through their own actions by merit of being mages - whether through the consequences of pursuing their Obsessions and being rewarded with arcane beats for making breakthroughs with them via doing dangerous or dubious stuff, being drawn into figuring out dangerous Mysteries and becoming involved in competition with other mages or supernatural communities, or through acts of Hubris when they get too comfortable or risk-prone with their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T09:54:19-07:00","id":1515675,"title":"","content":"Another suggestion: Sleeper witnesses. That can increase Paradox pools as well.<br /> <br /> My observations: Mages are pretty powerful even when they don't have time to prepare. Almost every starting Mage has one Arcana at 3 dots. The might have a hard time with certain challenges depending on Arcana spread amongst a cabal. If a player wanted to play one in another splat game I would seriously think about disallowing certain things for said character. For instance, I wouldn't allow a Spirit 3 Mage into a Werewolf game. Theoretically, a Spirit 3 Mage can control a Rank 5 Spirit. Could ruin a Werewolf game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T00:10:30-07:00","id":1515726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2/ Mages need to prepare: Mages are virtual demigods when they have time to prepare with rituals, but when caught unprepared they are vulnerable</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they <i>need</i> to prepare so much as preparation can be highly beneficial to them. Like, the right assemblage of Yantras and the time to make the ritual casting extensive, or the correct rote, can let them cover a lot of the bases that they want in a spell. But instant casting is always a possibility if necessary (and in an emergency, is likely to be the only thing you need to spend Reach on, so not necessarily a Paradox risk), and even if the dice pool is small there are a lot of impromptu situations where the factors don't need to be too high (especially if they get some steps in their primary factor for free). Besides, High Speech always affords a +2 dice bonus that can be utilised in practically every spell, albeit with the complications of losing the reflexive benefit of one's first Yantra and the likelihood of drawing attention from a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> Really, I'd say being unprepared is less a matter of the mage being especially vulnerable (although I've heard accounts of how players can just plain panic when caught off guard and forget about some of the effective countermeasures their Arcana might afford them, which seems to work very well in character) and more that there's higher risk of doing something that counts as an Act of Hubris. Getting one of the Conditions that comes with a failed roll there can cause... complications. As well as making the decision to contain potential Paradox more threatening (although the Condition you risk from it will last less time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3/ Mages have blind spots: My impression is that Mages can usually do some things really well, but are not that useful in others. For instance, a Mage with a high value in the Death Arcana would be great against Ghosts, but pretty hopeless when faced with a Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I'd ask first if the mage even has an Arcanum at an especially high level; given the Gnosis requirements to go above three dots, let alone all the way to five, it takes a lot of effort to become especially powerful as a mage. <br /> <br /> But sure, not every individual character can cover all of their bases, not every player group will have the full spread of Arcana, and while two or three dots are quite versatile they hardly cover every eventuality or let them exert themselves to the fullest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4/ Mages need Mana: My impression is that Mana is mainly used to prevent paradox due to reach (correct me if I am wrong), and that Mages can burn through it quickly through spell casting. They also need it for Healing (however limited). However, if they burn through their Mana reserves they are forced to confront Paradox which might blow up in their faces, or scourge their bodies which is very unhealthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the greater drains on mana might be casting improvised spells from outside one's Ruling Arcana, and it also provides a lot of use when scrutinising with Focused Mage Sight. Still, I think mana is primarily a matter of long term logistics; casting safely within one's Ruling Arcana is probably often straightforward enough, unless something particularly dire catches them by surprise.<br /> <br /> I think the major things that should be complications for the Awakened would be:<br /> <br /> * An assumption that they're generally going to want to understand Mysteries rather than treat them as things to break down, which can mean continuous contact with something that can be kind of hazardous, or at least make their lives more complicated.<br /> <br /> * Being involved with scenarios where there are a lot of moving parts, several of which involve people, in which there's not exactly some simple solution to line things up as they wish that won't cause a major disruption. Even if the characters/players are not very concerned with the ethics of that, such behaviour should risk their Wisdom (with attendant complications as mentioned before) and piss off other mages.<br /> <br /> * Other mages have their own claims on something that the player characters are interested in, or that are in the way of something they're interested in. Other spells, Consilium procedure and law, and simply the personality and agendas of those other mages can be something that players crash into in a manner that can cause blowback for them. You want to examine the ghosts in a graveyard, but there's a powerful Veiling over the place preventing that. You try dispelling it, and that's not just a crime against the mage who cast it and their cabal, it causes problems when something that wasn't supposed to be able to look at the graveyard now has a clear view of it. Maybe be cautious about any of your own critical long-term spells being abruptly broken in future.<br /> <br /> Besides all of that, I'd say that there are sometimes supernatural powers in the world where it's not entirely apparent what kinds of Arcana and Practices might provide countermeasures for what it might do to you or others, and even then the Clash of Wills roll might favour them. Plus, well... a lot of supernatural powers can be deployed more quickly and hit harder than an Awakened spell can in short order; there's no fiddling around with factors and Reach, no balancing bonuses and penalties to get all the moving parts in order, there's just an instant action, a strength based on number of successes rolled, and a tendency towards large dice polls to potentially afford a lot of them. And we've got enough examples of how exception based Mysteries can be that one can have cases where walking into the heart of something strange and fascinating to examine it can severely impair something that might be critical to a character.<br /> <br /> Never mind the likes of ruins of the Time Before, which seem to be built around an ethos of &quot;Indiana Jones traps where the trigger isn't stepping into the light, it's using certain spells&quot; and are structurally a bit proofed against the kinds of spells that would let one sequence break, before even considering the powerful guardian entity within that will have both Influence and Arcana and a free option to be either physical or ephemeral.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the capacity and versatility of Arcana are supposed to be things that let mages have their say or work their will in quite a lot of normal situations. It's just that being Addicted to Mystery inevitably draws them away from their comfort zones and across boundaries where the certainty of their power is less assured, for any number of reasons.<br /> <br /> Don't think of it as looking for the mage bane. Think of it as the things that might slap them across the face in their own particular idiom if mages get too close without proper precautions, and the consequences of their bad decisions (and how good decisions can be limiting in a way that frustrates and tempts).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T18:02:11-07:00","id":1515811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1515675#post1515675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, I wouldn't allow a Spirit 3 Mage into a Werewolf game. Theoretically, a Spirit 3 Mage can control a Rank 5 Spirit. Could ruin a Werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I glanced over the rules to check what might happen.<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 3, the mage can add +5 dice for ritual casting, if she takes 5 hours to cast it<br /> <br /> ...she can add 5 dice of Yantras, plus her Gnosis and Arcana can easily start at 6, for a grand total of 16 dice...<br /> <br /> ...if she makes the spell a Grimoire, Prime 1 (easy), it becomes a rote spell. She just needs to sacrifice 10 dice to overcome the rank 5 potency, but still doable at 6 dice. And all she needs to do is add 2 reach to issue a complex command, plus probably a bit to increase duration, but she will essentially have a rank 5 spirit to command?<br /> <br /> That is pretty crazy, did I miscalculate anything? Yes, I agree, that would certainly ruin a Werewolf game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T19:16:57-07:00","id":1515815,"title":"","content":"One button mis-pressed, taking away paragraphs of explaining how theoretical supremacy would remain only a theory in front of in-game context and judicious Storyteller management. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my point was that<br /> 1) in-game logistical issues make it actually not so easy for an average Joe to pull off that feat, and<br /> 2) you can play into the idea by <b>not</b> making the Spirit mage an average Jane, instead having the Spirit mage (preferably at Spirit 4 to 5, not 3) presented as a new and a serious threat to the local Shadow, and a potential archenemy of the pack (perhaps several packs).<br /> They still won\u2019t be playing Pokemon with Rank 4s and 5s, though! (Below that, on the other hand\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T19:47:11-07:00","id":1515817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1515811#post1515811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I glanced over the rules to check what might happen.<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 3, the mage can add +5 dice for ritual casting, if she takes 5 hours to cast it<br /> <br /> ...she can add 5 dice of Yantras, plus her Gnosis and Arcana can easily start at 6, for a grand total of 16 dice...<br /> <br /> ...if she makes the spell a Grimoire, Prime 1 (easy), it becomes a rote spell. She just needs to sacrifice 10 dice to overcome the rank 5 potency, but still doable at 6 dice. And all she needs to do is add 2 reach to issue a complex command, plus probably a bit to increase duration, but she will essentially have a rank 5 spirit to command?<br /> <br /> That is pretty crazy, did I miscalculate anything? Yes, I agree, that would certainly ruin a Werewolf game</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting from a grimoire doubles the casting time, which means your hypothetical god-leashing Disciple of Spirit needs to get their target to stay within her sensory range for ten hours for this brilliant plan to work. (If she doesn't know the rote, she can't use Scribe Grimoire to make a grimoire to get the rote quality on the casting in the first place.)<br /> <br /> If she's casting from across the Gauntlet without an open Iris to the Shadow, the Withstand for targeting a Rank 5 spirit needs Potency that ends up at more than 0 after subtracting 6 (and that's another Reach besides).<br /> <br /> The needs of the dicepool can be reduced somewhat by spending a Reach to switch the primary spell factor from Duration to Potency, but that's trading more dice for more potential for complications.<br /> <br /> The +2 Reach effect indicates that Spirit Summons is the spell we're talking about here, which means that the complex command is a single task described within a sentence or two; if you want to do a lot of different things with this near-godlike spirit, you need another casting or a different spell \u2014 the spell for &quot;make a spirit do as you tell it to&quot; is Command Spirit, which is Potency-primary but only allows you to command the spirit to perform a number of tasks equal to Potency (when Withstand reduces effective Potency, all the casting-time concerns for Spirit Summons still apply, and there's no inbuilt Reach option for casting across the Gauntlet, meaning you have to go to the thing or deal with the fact that casting on a target you can see across the Gauntlet costs 2 Reach for moving from Touch/Self range to Sensory range and casting remotely.)<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that most Rank 5 spirits out in the wild are not solitary creatures casually discovered on the street and it is reasonable to say the amount of legwork necessary for this nominally simple act of spellcasting to work without issue is the stuff whole stories are built out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T19:52:16-07:00","id":1515818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1515817#post1515817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting from a grimoire doubles the casting time, which means your hypothetical god-leashing Disciple of Spirit needs to get their target to stay within her sensory range for ten hours for this brilliant plan to work. (If she doesn't know the rote, she can't use Scribe Grimoire to make a grimoire to get the rote quality on the casting in the first place.)<br /> <br /> If she's casting from across the Gauntlet without an open Iris to the Shadow, the Withstand for targeting a Rank 5 spirit needs Potency that ends up at more than 0 after subtracting 6 (and that's another Reach besides).<br /> <br /> The needs of the dicepool can be reduced somewhat by spending a Reach to switch the primary spell factor from Duration to Potency, but that's trading more dice for more potential for complications.<br /> <br /> The +2 Reach effect indicates that Spirit Summons is the spell we're talking about here, which means that the complex command is a single task described within a sentence or two; if you want to do a lot of different things with this near-godlike spirit, you need another casting or a different spell \u2014 the spell for &quot;make a spirit do as you tell it to&quot; is Command Spirit, which is Potency-primary but only allows you to command the spirit to perform a number of tasks equal to Potency (when Withstand reduces effective Potency, all the casting-time concerns for Spirit Summons still apply, and there's no inbuilt Reach option for casting across the Gauntlet, meaning you have to go to the thing or deal with the fact that casting on a target you can see across the Gauntlet costs 2 Reach for moving from Touch/Self range to Sensory range and casting remotely.)<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that most Rank 5 spirits out in the wild are not solitary creatures casually discovered on the street and it is reasonable to say the amount of legwork necessary for this nominally simple act of spellcasting to work without issue is the stuff whole stories are built out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be mildly fair, it's totally fitting the arrogance of wizards to make that mistake.<br /> <br /> Players, on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:57:33-07:00","id":1515840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1515811#post1515811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I glanced over the rules to check what might happen.<br /> <br /> At Gnosis 3, the mage can add +5 dice for ritual casting, if she takes 5 hours to cast it<br /> <br /> ...she can add 5 dice of Yantras, plus her Gnosis and Arcana can easily start at 6, for a grand total of 16 dice...<br /> <br /> ...if she makes the spell a Grimoire, Prime 1 (easy), it becomes a rote spell. She just needs to sacrifice 10 dice to overcome the rank 5 potency, but still doable at 6 dice. And all she needs to do is add 2 reach to issue a complex command, plus probably a bit to increase duration, but she will essentially have a rank 5 spirit to command?<br /> <br /> That is pretty crazy, did I miscalculate anything? Yes, I agree, that would certainly ruin a Werewolf game</div> </div> </div> </div>One clarification, the 5 dice cap on yantra bonus is after you subtract for spell factor penalties. Since you subtracted 10 you are at a net -5 and can add upto +10 more dice in yantra bonuses ...<br /> <br /> So in this example that actual cap is how do you get 3 yantra slots to +15 dice (pretty sure this is not possible). The best i can come up with is +6 rote mundra (requires knowing the rote, having 5 dots in the rote skill, and having that skill be an order rote specialization), +4 persona bonus (requires a relevant shadow name merit at 3 dots and a relevant cabal theme merit at 1 dot), and +3 for the third slot (which could be an appropriate sacrament which required a quest to another realm, or a soul stone from a higher Gnosis mage). <br /> <br /> Which totals a hell of a lot of specialization in this particular spell (rote) and sligthly more general thematically appropriate character development (for the persona benefits) and arguably more investment of time and effort to justify getting them soul stone/sacrament.<br /> <br /> But capping at a theoretical +13 (+16 if you had another yantra slot to use both soul stone and sacrament and took 6 spell factor steps) - Gnosis 3 + spirit 3 + 13 yantra bonus, -10 spell factors = 9 dice.<br /> <br /> At which point, I don't think you would need to do a double lenght ritual casting for the extra +5 ritual casting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T06:16:52-07:00","id":1515856,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that a Rank 5 spirit is practically a force of nature. If they know who has the universal remote to their powers, they might want to send their choir to deal with them.<br /> <br /> While the spirit is busy, others may capitalize to attack its power base, which can shift the local balance of power.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there might be spirit occultists and Purified (full or prospective) that may not take kindly to having a major sponsor being highjacked.<br /> <br /> The big challenge is how well the mage considered and prepared for the consequences.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T15:12:52-07:00","id":1515900,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like, a story featuring mages with the Spirit Arcanum and werewolves isn't one where the werewolves mope about how there's something else that can kind of not really bind spirits more easily than they can. From the werewolf point of view, it's about this group of people who aren't part of the ecology of the Shadow who seem to be pulling spirits out of place and messing up the careful balance of power over there.<br /> <br /> That makes those people prey.<br /> <br /> As I said, things that slap you in the face for your hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:33:38-07:00","id":1516471,"title":"","content":"One thing that doesn't come up often is that you can actually, at least temporarily, *take a mage's magic away*. It is completely thematically appropriate and setting-compliant to have rituals, disciplines, gifts, rites, and dread powers that make magic more difficult. I have 100 suggestions for balancing mages mechanically and narratively but never forget that the most terrifying part of being a mage is that you can be severed from your power. And in fact, there's probably a rich ecosystem of things out there that do just that...<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:43:12-07:00","id":1516472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516471#post1516471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that doesn't come up often is that you can actually, at least temporarily, *take a mage's magic away*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is completely thematically appropriate and setting-compliant to have rituals, disciplines, gifts, rites, and dread powers that make magic more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that they can bring out competing effects that force Clash of Wills, sure, but I don't believe there is anything that can shut Awakened magic down outright, nor do I find it particularly thematic or setting matching.<br /> <br /> Like, how is blood magic supposed to do anything to a connection to the Supernal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have 100 suggestions for balancing mages mechanically and narratively but never forget that the most terrifying part of being a mage is that you can be severed from your power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any example of such to leave mages so terrified?<br /> <br /> That's apart from the matter of how, from what I gather, people in general will just regard the challenge of &quot;your cool powers just get cut off entirely&quot; as the lamest possible thing.<br /> <br /> (I draw a distinction between that and Mysteries that run interference on very specific applications of power; like, there's stuff you can't use the Time Arcanum for on a Mummy, and plenty of stuff that you can.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:57:12-07:00","id":1516539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I normally hang around the Werewolf Forms, but I have a keen interest in all the Chronicles of Darkness games. I wanted to ask how to make life\u2026challenging\u2026 for Mages. I get that Mages are arguably the most powerful entities in the Chronicles of Darkness, but I imagine that they must have some weaknesses. I am sorry if this thread was done to death in the past but I am curious</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1/ Mages are Squishy: The most obvious point is that Mages are just ordinary people when you look at it and break easy. Sure they can get Mage armor, but some of the mage armors are tougher than others and using Mana to heal is very inefficient compared to other splats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2/ Mages need to prepare: Mages are virtual demigods when they have time to prepare with rituals, but when caught unprepared they are vulnerable</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3/ Mages have blind spots: My impression is that Mages can usually do some things really well, but are not that useful in others. For instance, a Mage with a high value in the Death Arcana would be great against Ghosts, but pretty hopeless when faced with a Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4/ Mages need Mana: My impression is that Mana is mainly used to prevent paradox due to reach (correct me if I am wrong), and that Mages can burn through it quickly through spell casting. They also need it for Healing (however limited). However, if they burn through their Mana reserves they are forced to confront Paradox which might blow up in their faces, or scourge their bodies which is very unhealthy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know if I am missing anything. </span></span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949443-sleeper-curiosity-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-labyrinth\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949443-sleeper-curiosity-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-labyrinth\"> Sleeper Curiosity, or How I Learned To Stop Worrying and Love the Labyrinth - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949443-sleeper-curiosity-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-labyrinth\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949443-sleeper-curiosity-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-labyrinth </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, I was reading the Hurt Locker previews again and was struck by a small epiphany that there might be some new interesting piece to add to Mage's mechanics. This </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is pretty old but this mechanizes sleeper curiosity and makes a bit more interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:43:12-07:00","id":1516613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516472#post1516472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they can bring out competing effects that force Clash of Wills, sure, but I don't believe there is anything that can shut Awakened magic down outright, nor do I find it particularly thematic or setting matching.<br /> <br /> Like, how is blood magic supposed to do anything to a connection to the Supernal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Among published materials, Sorcerous Eunuch and the Crusade Style both targets magic in general. The latter can be used to straight up deny use of the Mantra or interrupt the casting of any spell (that takes more than one turn to cast).<br /> So while shutting down specifically Awakened magic might be difficult to justify, there are precedents for making it more difficult to cast spells in general.<br /> You've already mentioned competing effects, but note that such effects can be pretty wide ranging. For example, Apocalypse (Theban Sorcery) could make all Veiling spells impossible to cast for an area potentially covering miles, for a whole week.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Apocalypse is insane because that's not even a CoW. Illusions just straight up doesn't work within that area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-29-2023, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T03:22:43-07:00","id":1516625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516613#post1516613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter can be used to straight up deny use of the Mantra</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean as in one yantra out of several?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">interrupt the casting of any spell (that takes more than one turn to cast).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think interruption is fair game so long as it's something that takes up an action for every action one wants to negate.<br /> <br /> Depending on exactly what you mean, more details would not go amiss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Apocalypse (Theban Sorcery) could make all Veiling spells impossible to cast for an area potentially covering miles, for a whole week.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Apocalypse is insane because that's not even a CoW. Illusions just straight up doesn't work within that area.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I think the Clash of Wills rules are pretty fundamental in a manner that implicitly takes precedent without anything needing to say in every instance that a Clash of Wills occurs.<br /> <br /> If it has some kind of specific wording that says that such powers don't work without even the benefit of Clash of Wills (or some other mechanism to be opposed, a minimum number of successes or something; Clash can be foregone if a power already references a way to resolve the conflict), then it's already not playing by the rules and ought to be ignored.<br /> <br /> Besides, I wouldn't think every form of Veiling constitutes an illusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T08:48:19-07:00","id":1516656,"title":"","content":"Some weaknesses not already mentioned<br /> <br /> Wisdom: Mages that run roughshod over people, killing, maiming and manipulating others tend to suffer wisdom loss (MtAw p 87). Read that section very carefully, especially the top of p 88 where it says you can not spend willpower to assist the roll to avoid wisdom loss. Wisdom costs arcane experience to replace, standard experience will not help. The standard level of wisdom is the four to to seven range, with two of the sins being &quot;allowing a sleeper to witness obvious magic&quot;, or &quot;forcing a being to act counter to its interests&quot;. Also, the lower wisdom gets, the worse paradox gets. Glossing over points like these, especially in a crossover game, can allow mages to seem much more powerful than they are.<br /> <br /> Mages are specialists: It's not just about paths of magic, each has two areas of reality they are strong in and one they are really handicapped. This means that while a spirit mage can easily figure out what's going on with spirits, and a death mage can see right through a ghost plot, you hit either of them with a computer hacking astral entity and they will be helpless. There are also three dramatic systems in chronicles of darkness, combat, social maneuvering and investigation. Each mage is also part of an order that will be strong in one of those systems but weak in the other two. Keep in mind, it costs a lot of experience to be a powerful mage, reducing the amount of experience that mage can spend on stats and skills. <br /> <br /> Double lives: A mage has a Shadow name (his magical persona) and a Sympathetic name (normal human identity). Learning the Sympathetic name of a powerful mage gives you a great deal of leverage over that mage. Giving that name to a mage's enemies can make their life miserable very quickly. A more subtle check on a mages power would be to invite a mages family member, close friend, or work associate to an event you don't want tampered with. If the mage you don't want around shows up and starts blasting with obvious magic, well, he's done your work for you. <br /> <br /> Buffs: Many mages like to enhance their abilities with long lasting spells. These buffs give mages stats, skills, and merits for free, until the spell runs out. Your solution, magical traps that turn these buffs against them. Also consider monsters that like to eat magic, and mages. There are many such creatures in the lower depths<br /> <br /> In any crossover campaign I would recommend limiting the gnosis of player character mages to one until a major story goal is completed. Then allow gnosis to two until the next milestone and so on. This will limit power gaming, especially if buff eating traps and monsters are prevalent.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T10:35:38-07:00","id":1516670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516656#post1516656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are specialists: It's not just about paths of magic, each has two areas of reality they are strong in and one they are really handicapped. This means that while a spirit mage can easily figure out what's going on with spirits, and a death mage can see right through a ghost plot, you hit either of them with a computer hacking astral entity and they will be helpless. There are also three dramatic systems in chronicles of darkness, combat, social maneuvering and investigation. Each mage is also part of an order that will be strong in one of those systems but weak in the other two. Keep in mind, it costs a lot of experience to be a powerful mage, reducing the amount of experience that mage can spend on stats and skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of this isn't really a mage thing so much as a &quot;characters acting in a system where they won't be able to spread their dots evenly across everything they can do&quot; thing. Like, if you select normal humans where none of them have Computers, they're going to be disadvantaged in computer hacking challenges, that doesn't really make absolutely everybody a specialist in a way that's worth commenting on.<br /> <br /> I think people can overstate the significance of Inferior Arcana; for one thing, it's not until you want to buy the third dot of the thing that you run into the constraints of slightly higher XP cost and needing a teacher (and for a lot of practical considerations, the teacher can be... other members of the mage's cabal).<br /> <br /> And all of the Orders have decent capability in social, combat, and investigation matters. Like, the last especially, all mages are concerned with investigation of one kind or another. There's a lot more nuance in how they function than just their one sentence summary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double lives: A mage has a Shadow name (his magical persona) and a Sympathetic name (normal human identity). Learning the Sympathetic name of a powerful mage gives you a great deal of leverage over that mage. Giving that name to a mage's enemies can make their life miserable very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>A powerful mage can probably cast a decent ward over themselves.<br /> <br /> Knowing the sympathetic name is an advantage, but hardly a disaster. In some respects it's most useful for being able to serve as the sympathetic yantra to cast a spell at range in the first place, freeing up stuff other things to provide the actual dice bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more subtle check on a mages power would be to invite a mages family member, close friend, or work associate to an event you don't want tampered with. If the mage you don't want around shows up and starts blasting with obvious magic, well, he's done your work for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Smart mages tend not to show up and blast around with obvious magic even if there's a rumble in the abandoned warehouse district.<br /> <br /> It is so easy for mages to turn invisible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your solution, magical traps that turn these buffs against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also consider monsters that like to eat magic, and mages. There are many such creatures in the lower depths</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things are challenging to get a hold of even for the Awakened who know about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any crossover campaign I would recommend limiting the gnosis of player character mages to one until a major story goal is completed. Then allow gnosis to two until the next milestone and so on. This will limit power gaming, especially if buff eating traps and monsters are prevalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosis is already a pretty expensive trait, this seems an unnecessary constriction.<br /> <br /> Like, it's already going to take until Gnosis 3 before they can buy so much as one Arcanum up to four dots, what would you be worried about?<br /> <br /> (And a whole bunch of things you're bringing up have absolutely already been mentioned)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T10:25:56-07:00","id":1516981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516472#post1516472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply! I would recommend taking a look at the Septemi bloodline from 1E Ancient Bloodlines (or the conversion in Bloodlines the Resurrected on STV). This is an entire bloodline that makes it almost impossible for mages to use magic. More importantly than that maybe, it expands the design space of the Chronicles of Darkness to include creatures and abilities that specifically abjure supernatural/magical abilities. You can use the Septemi themselves, or maybe Septemi vitae as an abjuration plot device, or similar Gifts/Rites/etc. Night Horrors also include creatures that mess with the soul or the abyss and make things more horrifying for mages to be mages.<br /> <br /> What I was trying to convey with my first point is that even without Gifts, a werewolf can Change. Even without Disciplines, vampires are resilient and can call on their vitae or the Beast... but without Arcana, mages are quite literally just humans.<br /> <br /> In mechanical terms, I use two homebrew changes that make Mages much more palatable for any kind of crossover (as PCs or NPCs):<ul><li>All improvised spells cost 1 mana (praxes/rotes free unless other cost stated)</li> <li>Ruling arcana spells get -1 paradox dice. If you join a Legacy whose Ruling Arcanum is already one of your own, that arcanum gets -2 paradox dice.</li> </ul>Combined with the character creation rules from Signs of Sorcery, I've found it actually goes 90% of the way towards &quot;balancing&quot; mages. Paradox isn't a meaningful disincentive for most mages, in fact canonically some wear paradox &quot;like a badge of honor.&quot; But having to be judicious about the improvised magic they use actually makes mage adversaries much more reasonable opponents for your players, and forces mage players to make more interesting decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 07-02-2023, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T14:08:16-07:00","id":1516999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516981#post1516981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but without Arcana, mages are quite literally just humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to get my thoughts together for the thread on the whole, but this needs a quick address, because, uh. No, they're not.<br /> <br /> Even if we start from the Newly Awakened Mage template, a mage who, for whatever reason, doesn't cast magic, still has an inhuman Aspiration in the form of an Obsession, has the ability to Scour their Pattern for Mana and then spend it for healing in a way that allows them to juggle some of the consequences of any physical violence they encounter, do not suffer from the same psychological (or spiritual) damage as humans on account of Wisdom not being Integrity, casually inflicts Nimbus on their regular places and can willfully inflict their immediate Nimbus with an expenditure of Mana, are affected by and can utilize Mage Sight, can partition their souls off and can use it to imbue an area with Supernal resonance, has a a metaphysical armor they can call up at will, and likely has an Attainment that changes the way they interact with casual reality.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't take my usual (and admitted) extreme of treating mages as non-humans, the fact remains that these are not things a human can do. Even if you want to take it as a mage without casting magic is on par with a human with a number of supernatural merits, it's enough of a package that if you have one of each tackling the same problems, one's going to have a distinct edge of handling it over the other, and it certainly makes a difference in the way that a mage, making the mistake of thinking of themselves as &quot;just human&quot; is, over a long enough period of time, is going to have to ask what the fuck is wrong with every other human that they can't handle the same situations they do, and the fallout that comes from not recognizing such a platform.<br /> <br /> It's a trap for anyone dealing with them as well-while a castingless mage is relying on Mana possibly more regularly than a casting mage, and thus that's a factor, anyone who conflicts with a mage like they do a human is going to find themselves falling short, and it's that gap in expectations where mages tend to become a problem for everyone else-and themselves, down the long way.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, &quot;mages are quite literally just humans&quot; is a great way to get shot by mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-02-2023, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T14:49:16-07:00","id":1517003,"title":"","content":"Hah, fair. I will refer you to the disclaimer in my signature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was lumping Attainments in with the associated Arcana, as they're similarly affected by clash of wills but I suppose you'd have to make a determination as to how that interacts with abjuration-style abilities. In my experience, once you take away spells/attainments, what's left is very pale in comparison to the other splats, and is even possible for a mortal to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T15:09:23-07:00","id":1517006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516981#post1516981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the late reply! I would recommend taking a look at the Septemi bloodline from 1E Ancient Bloodlines (or the conversion in Bloodlines the Resurrected on STV). This is an entire bloodline that makes it almost impossible for mages to use magic. More importantly than that maybe, it expands the design space of the Chronicles of Darkness to include creatures and abilities that specifically abjure supernatural/magical abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of being able to evaluate these mechanics directly, I can only comment that this sounds at best like something designed solely for its own context, and not readily reconciled with Awakening.<br /> <br /> At worst, it's mere power creep.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T15:23:49-07:00","id":1517008,"title":"","content":"True, if you're looking for something inherent to Mage without any of the other sourcebooks, I think everyone else here has covered every avenue. Using a VtR sourcebook to scope possibilities in Mage is a lot like using the Spirit information from Forsaken in Mage... you could completely disregard it, but there's lots of fruitful space in the intersection...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T05:52:38-07:00","id":1517056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517008#post1517008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, if you're looking for something inherent to Mage without any of the other sourcebooks, I think everyone else here has covered every avenue. Using a VtR sourcebook to scope possibilities in Mage is a lot like using the Spirit information from Forsaken in Mage... you could completely disregard it, but there's lots of fruitful space in the intersection...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's completely different; Werewolf: the Forsaken heavily elaborates on the Shadow, which is significant for mages when one of the Ruling Arcana of one of their Paths is focused on interaction with it. A vampire source book describing how an obscure power can totally shut down the Awakened is far more tangential, and should be held to higher scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Still, the Clash of Wills rules are there to resolve such things. It's okay to have some power that can run some form of resistance so long as it's possible to struggle against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T09:15:08-07:00","id":1517078,"title":"","content":"Deviants have a few powers that can be used to interefere with Mage abilities, and giving Vampires (especially a specific bloodline), Changelings, or what have you abilities that let them more directly clash against Mages or, say, apply an inherent Withstand bonus to the area isn't problematic per se, but it should be used rarely and sparingly, primarily a Mystery rather than a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T12:05:36-07:00","id":1517086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517078#post1517078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviants have a few powers that can be used to interefere with Mage abilities, and giving Vampires (especially a specific bloodline), Changelings, or what have you abilities that let them more directly clash against Mages or, say, apply an inherent Withstand bonus to the area isn't problematic per se, but it should be used rarely and sparingly, primarily a Mystery rather than a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's okay to reference such things as part of a larger conversation, but should be regarded as outliers, lest it become an advice of &quot;challenge mages by assembling every obscure thing with a particular power that happens to interfere with their magic specifically and make this the luckiest damn cabal there ever was&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's important to focus a discussion on the challenges that exist when mages are able to use their powers as normal, because it allows some back and forth, or presents something that can have the powers be employed for creative problem solving. Lean too heavily on the idea of beings with the ability to directly counter or inhibit magic, and it's basically saying that mages are too inconvenient to make compelling challenges for, so you have to challenge them by temporarily making them not mages.<br /> <br /> On a tangential note, I think there are valid points about what mages still have when they're not using their spells, but think that a lot of those things have a lot less utility than, say, a vampire or werewolf retains if not using their purchased powers. Most of those things have very subtle effects (Long-term Nimbus especially is basically just cosmetic before you hit higher Gnosis, and isn't affecting most stuff in your life if you're doing a Shadow Name properly).<br /> <br /> And I don't quite buy that pattern restoration would change the mage attitude towards violence, beyond maybe a sense that they can possibly have an emergency out if necessary that still comes at great cost to them in terms of a resource that could probably have been more useful for something else. It's not like vampire and werewolf regeneration (and downgrading lethal to bashing damage). Plus, pattern scouring yourself for it... I feel as though characters should at times be played as though they're averse to things that are painful to them even if there's no long term damage or dice penalty to represent debilitating pain.<br /> <br /> Plus, for the majority of mages, they can do that once per day to reap the exact amount of mana that can fix one level of damage, so... it's more like juggling a knife than a ball, as far as interaction with violence goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T12:13:24-07:00","id":1517089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517086#post1517086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's okay to reference such things as part of a larger conversation, but should be regarded as outliers, lest it become an advice of &quot;challenge mages by assembling every obscure thing with a particular power that happens to interfere with their magic specifically and make this the luckiest damn cabal there ever was&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, as I said, one-off or rare Mysteries, not a typical challenge.<br /> <br /> Though, the broader context, I feel, is that Mage doesn't shine as a combat centric game. The challenge shouldn't be that spells don't work to insta-gib your enemies, but that insta-gibbing people should rarely be a useful solution to a problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T18:51:05-07:00","id":1517126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517056#post1517056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's completely different; Werewolf: the Forsaken heavily elaborates on the Shadow, which is significant for mages when one of the Ruling Arcana of one of their Paths is focused on interaction with it. A vampire source book describing how an obscure power can totally shut down the Awakened is far more tangential, and should be held to higher scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Still, the Clash of Wills rules are there to resolve such things. It's okay to have some power that can run some form of resistance so long as it's possible to struggle against.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to note that Kvark is <i>extremely</i> overselling how Abjurism works, both in the original Ancient Bloodlines writeup and in NMD's update in Bloodlines: the Resurrected.<br /> <br /> The original writeup presents a ladder of effects allowing the character to, in order, raise their resistance to supernatural powers for one turn, banish generally-perceived sensory illusions, remove targeted mind-affecting supernatural effects, banish summoned entities, and end supernatural effects.<br /> <br /> The 2e rewrite works like one of the physical Disciplines, with a Persistent effect adding Abjurism dots to the character's Resistance Attributes for the purposes of contesting supernatural powers (i.e. they have functionally higher Withstand ratings) and Active effects allowing them to force a Clash against supernatural powers or Manifestations/Embodiments to suppress them for a duration based on their Abjurism dots (effectively starting out measured in turns and proceeding along the CofD narrative time units progression to cap at permanent suppression with five dots).<br /> <br /> Worth remembering that the Clash of Wills rules are how basically every gameline's equivalent of Dispel Magic works in the first place and that &quot;include supernatural creatures who can undo supernatural effects&quot; is not exactly the most useful advice for how to make life challenging for mages save in the sense that it's an extra reason for them to avoid spending resources on non-guaranteed outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T20:06:52-07:00","id":1517239,"title":"","content":"I don't know how much it's an overstatement, they have an active ability that allows them to permanently suppress any supernatural (incl Awakened) power. But I'm less interested in any one specific adversary or bloodline than in the general concept that there is likely a wide variety of (maybe rare?) things in the CofD world that are adept at specifically shutting down magical/supernatural abilities. That bloodline for sure, but likely also lodges, Spirits, banishers, left-handed legacies, etc. Whether or not that's useful or interesting to you and your campaign, I think it's worth not overlooking.<br /> <br /> If that's not your thing, 1e had a rich menagerie of adversaries that specifically made life hard for mages, like the Metatron that hunted mages that abused Fate magic and had special abilities for dealing with them. I feel like it's a very intentional part of the cosmology as a concept, but obviously I can't say for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T12:41:15-07:00","id":1517299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1516656#post1516656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some weaknesses not already mentioned<br /> <br /> Wisdom: Mages that run roughshod over people, killing, maiming and manipulating others tend to suffer wisdom loss (MtAw p 87). Read that section very carefully, especially the top of p 88 where it says you can not spend willpower to assist the roll to avoid wisdom loss. Wisdom costs arcane experience to replace, standard experience will not help. The standard level of wisdom is the four to to seven range, with two of the sins being &quot;allowing a sleeper to witness obvious magic&quot;, or &quot;forcing a being to act counter to its interests&quot;. Also, the lower wisdom gets, the worse paradox gets. Glossing over points like these, especially in a crossover game, can allow mages to seem much more powerful than they are.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea... I think you nailed it here. This was something I had a feeling was a huge constraint on mages. Reading that section on Wisdom, it seems that your average mage, with a Wisdom of 4 to 7, will roll 3 dice to check against Wisdom loss if he does anything like let sleepers see him, not contain a Paradox, or control someone (which covers lots of powers, especially with mind). Statistically, this means that they will fail approximately 1 in 3 times. When they do fail, they become megalomaniacal, or Rampant, which I consider the gentler, kinder, Mage equivalent of Werewolf Kuruth which is when the Mage decides to take over the world and use his powers indiscriminately, probably eroding his Wisdom further.<br /> <br /> Another big issue is regarding Supernal Entities. If you kill one than you have committed the worst Wisdom loss crime and therefore roll 1 dice to lose Wisdom. The problem is that, if a Supernal Entity starts attacking you, you basically can do nothing but run and hide. This was also mentioned in Signs and Sorcery when it talks about the minions of the Exarchs. They have legions of Supernal Entities to wield against the Mages (and they are really powerful if I understand their mechanics correctly), and the mages cannot destroy them without losing lots of Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T15:17:38-07:00","id":1517313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517299#post1517299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have legions of Supernal Entities to wield against the Mages</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exarchs don't throw around power indiscriminately, and Supernal Entities still have limited time and range to survive in the Fallen World. They're not being tossed all over the place.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery actually does put it into proper perspective; for the most part, the specific members of the Pentacle Orders are beneath the notice of the Exarchs, grudge work delegated to the help. Being a direct target of an Ochema or other Supernal Entity under the direction of the Thrones is mostly a case of bad luck, stumbling upon some arcane agenda beyond your comprehension but where your interference or the offence given is responded to with the most severe force.<br /> <br /> Seers of the Throne are willing to wield Supernal Entities against their enemies, but that still generally requires summoning, with all of the usual inconveniences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T19:02:31-07:00","id":1517323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517299#post1517299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they do fail, they become megalomaniacal, or Rampant, which I consider the gentler, kinder, Mage equivalent of Werewolf Kuruth which is when the Mage decides to take over the world and use his powers indiscriminately, probably eroding his Wisdom further.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparisons I've made before are that Rampant is the existing thing to point to when people say Mage's toolkit for steering players toward playing characters in a particular direction is mostly carrots rather than sticks \u2014 the wake-up call for that Condition is generally reaching beyond your grasp or using magic in front of Sleepers, and the more magically capable you are the more the latter becomes the most expedient resolution that may simply repeat itself in a subsequent loss of Wisdom until you hit the Falling threshold \u2014 and Megalomaniacal's resolution criteria are basically in the same category as Vampire puts for ending a frenzy you dramatically failed to resist (whether normally or by failing to ride the wave) \u2014 that new Vice and Obsession and lack of mundane Empathy are stuck with you until you hurt someone close to you in a way that risks further Wisdom loss, which is a fantastic reason to try and keep your Wisdom above the level where that entails less extreme things than impulse killings or mutilation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T14:30:08-07:00","id":1517406,"title":"","content":"Just one question this raises:<br /> <br /> Pattern Restoration allows a Mage spend three mana to (among other things) remove a mental condition (without gaining a beat).<br /> <br /> So while sub-optimal (for XP gain) can't and rampant/megalomaniac mage just spend 3 mana (if the character realises they are suffering from a mental condition)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T15:13:02-07:00","id":1517409,"title":"","content":"Technically a Mind Mage can do the same with <u>Clear Thoughts</u>.<br /> <br /> Unless, in either case, you gained them through the Dramatic Failure Wisdom roll effect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T15:19:06-07:00","id":1517413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517409#post1517409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically a Mind Mage can do the same with <u>Clear Thoughts</u>.<br /> <br /> Unless, in either case, you gained them through the Dramatic Failure Wisdom roll effect</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i had not thought of that. So clear thoughts is great for clearing someone else's condition (with the reach option for lasting). Which works for when they don't want to fix it themselves...<br /> <br /> Of course, a Mage player playing the megalomaniac condition probably has their character think everything is fine, they are just awesome...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T15:21:58-07:00","id":1517414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517413#post1517413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which works for when they don't want to fix it themselves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just, y'know, be careful how you go about it. Casting a spell on an unwilling Mage is always a risky prospect. Good way to get Frayed. Could always sell it to them as &quot;hey, let me restore some WP for you&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T15:48:14-07:00","id":1517417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517414#post1517414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just, y'know, be careful how you go about it. Casting a spell on an unwilling Mage is always a risky prospect. Good way to get Frayed. Could always sell it to them as &quot;hey, let me restore some WP for you&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, their Prime Shielding effect probably adds a withstand for all harmful spells, so they may just assume it isn't harmful if you don't put much potency in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-07-2023, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T16:02:32-07:00","id":1517420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517417#post1517417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, their Prime Shielding effect probably adds a withstand for all harmful spells, so they may just assume it isn't harmful if you don't out much potency in...</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Wards and Signs</u> makes no distinction between harmful and non-harmful, all shall be Withstood! Seriously though, unless one added a Key to it, Prime Shielding is fairly indiscriminate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T19:13:57-07:00","id":1517440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517406#post1517406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one question this raises:<br /> <br /> Pattern Restoration allows a Mage spend three mana to (among other things) remove a mental condition (without gaining a beat).<br /> <br /> So while sub-optimal (for XP gain) can't and rampant/megalomaniac mage just spend 3 mana (if the character realises they are suffering from a mental condition)?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that this is an obviously non-permissible resolution for the same reason that Paradox Conditions cannot reasonably be concluded to be resolvable by scouring them before they've settled into your Pattern, as well as because the book never fully defines a Mental Condition and Mind is only one of three Arcana with a core published spell that messes with Obsessions as both Rampant and Megalomaniacal do.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic can't remove Scars from Deviants, directly mess with a Sin-Eater's Synergy, or give direct increases to a soul's Integrity or Wisdom, so I wouldn't allow a template feature that exists well below the level of spellcasting to get rid of a Condition as entwined with the game's systems for how your magic spreads and affects how much control you have over it. Pattern Restoration can help you purge a lingering Guilty consciense or being Swooned by a mind-twisting dream-creature, but the direct consequences of a failure of your magical self-control should not be able to be bought off for the price of healing a minor animal bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:02:38-07:00","id":1517456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517440#post1517440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading is that this is an obviously non-permissible resolution for the same reason that Paradox Conditions cannot reasonably be concluded to be resolvable by scouring them before they've settled into your Pattern, as well as because the book never fully defines a Mental Condition and Mind is only one of three Arcana with a core published spell that messes with Obsessions as both Rampant and Megalomaniacal do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an okay interpretation, but I find a lot of reasonable basis to think of Obsessions and those Conditions as largely psychological things, on top of a sense that Acts of Hubris can be so common and those Conditions exert such a particular influence on character actions that it's not unreasonable for them to have a way out of it (albeit a somewhat costly one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the direct consequences of a failure of your magical self-control should not be able to be bought off for the price of healing a minor animal bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that metric for the value of it is off, because Pattern Restoration is explicitly supposed to be really bad regeneration. Like, it being the cost of healing an animal bite does not mean that the value of three mana is low, it just means that physical Pattern Restoration is just about the least efficient thing you can spend your mana on.<br /> <br /> Certainly, healing a minor animal bite is not equivalent to the value of three improvised spells from Common and Inferior Arcana.<br /> <br /> At the same time, mental Pattern Restoration exists in an intended design space in which the Awakened have a lot of authority over their own head space (even if on the whole it's probably still not the best use of that much mana).<br /> <br /> I don't think it necessarily trivialises the consequences of losing Wisdom, because a lot of what is supposed to be bad there is the Act of Hubris itself, there are still the effects that it has on Paradox, and one could incorporate such a loop into a character who keeps evading the psychological toll of Hubris in a way that means that they never learn anything from it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T09:03:30-07:00","id":1517495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517456#post1517456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it necessarily trivialises the consequences of losing Wisdom, because a lot of what is supposed to be bad there is the Act of Hubris itself, there are still the effects that it has on Paradox, and one could incorporate such a loop into a character who keeps evading the psychological toll of Hubris in a way that means that they never learn anything from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a much longer post written up going through comparisons to Humanity and Integrity, but suffice it to say that I do not believe the game's primary means of modeling &quot;mages who act unWisely can be given to self-absorbed power-tripping and exhibiting more magical ability than sense&quot; should be able to be gotten rid of without their resolution's narrative reality-check for less trouble than it takes a vampire to heal from the heat of a first-degree burn by using the template feature that exists to ensure they can regain control of their faculties and emotions, particularly not when Obsessions exist in the same subset of character sheet elements that CofD uses to model the hungers of bluebook Horrors, the drives of Remade Symbiotes, and the intended destiny a player has for their character which they are not necessarily privy to, regardless of these elements having contact with the character's psychology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T10:18:22-07:00","id":1517500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517495#post1517495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a much longer post written up going through comparisons to Humanity and Integrity, but suffice it to say that I do not believe the game's primary means of modeling &quot;mages who act unWisely can be given to self-absorbed power-tripping and exhibiting more magical ability than sense&quot; should be able to be gotten rid of without their resolution's narrative reality-check for less trouble than it takes a vampire to heal from the heat of a first-degree burn by using the template feature that exists to ensure they can regain control of their faculties and emotions</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a necessary place to reconcile &quot;self-absorbed power tripping and being less than sensible&quot; with regaining control of faculties and emotions.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the use in trying to find other examples of things to establish some sort of baseline value to units, because I don't really see such a thing as intended to be consistent across the games; it's like parsing the preciousness of a Mentor against an Artifact when they both cost five dots, that's not really the point. Whatever it costs a vampire to heal the damage inflicted by one of their Banes, that's a thing that purely exists in its own narrative space of how they deal with physical injury and the necessities of recovering their power points, it doesn't establish some common baseline across all games.<br /> <br /> In the case of mages, it's not about going through all the details to figure out what the precise worth of each point of Mana is, it's &quot;do I have the Hallow/tass access or am I willing to take that point of lethal damage that can't be magically healed to recoup the cost of fixing this thing, when I might need that for mitigating Paradox later&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">particularly not when Obsessions exist in the same subset of character sheet elements that CofD uses to model the hungers of bluebook Horrors, the drives of Remade Symbiotes, and the intended destiny a player has for their character which they are not necessarily privy to, regardless of these elements having contact with the character's psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Horror hungers another take on Aspirations or something they have in addition to Aspirations that gets included in their rules in Hunter Second Edition? Although you're saying the blue book, but I can't find any description there of them having anything other than Aspirations (even if the animalistic ones might merely Aspire to satisfy certain appetites). Either way, I'm not really seeing the case for that being anything other than a psychological phenomenon in its own right.<br /> <br /> Same with what I am inferring about the fact that some Deviants have multiple consciousnesses that come with separate Aspirations.<br /> <br /> And sure, Obsessions don't always represent conscious, deliberate goals and drives of a character, but they often do. Considering the elements described in those Conditions, I think the Obsessions they force of &quot;dominate others&quot; and &quot;use magic indiscriminately&quot; can be considered wilful rather than signalling the Storyteller to bring things into contact with them.<br /> <br /> Are the impulses of Horrors and that subset of Deviants not the kind of thing that is subject to the Mind Arcanum? Are they off limits to Psychic Reprogramming?<br /> <br /> I feel as though the worst that could be proposed about them is that they're rules that don't seem to be cross-referencing one another and might come across as at odds, but as it is Megalomaniacal and Rampant lack the language that would make them a more supernatural kind of Condition like Soulless or Soul Shocked, in a way that makes them come out as Mental to the same extent as Amnesia or Fugue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T11:56:54-07:00","id":1517509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517500#post1517500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a necessary place to reconcile &quot;self-absorbed power tripping and being less than sensible&quot; with regaining control of faculties and emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and getting an Obsession rewritten, gaining an extra Vice, and not being able to successfully use your normal Empathy are not what I would term a loss of faculties or control of one's emotions. These are Conditions that can be made Persistent and obviously are not constantly affecting the character's thought process outside of extremely broad and deep magical talents, which definitionally have more room for other Obsessions to operate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't see the use in trying to find other examples of things to establish some sort of baseline value to units, </div> </div> </div>That is not my intention, else I'd be going over the fact that Improved Pattern Restoration only affects the costs for healing damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever it costs a vampire to heal the damage inflicted by one of their Banes, that's a thing that purely exists in its own narrative space of how they deal with physical injury and the necessities of recovering their power points, it doesn't establish some common baseline across all games. </div> </div> </div>I make the comparison because I consider the consideration of a Condition that is only acquired from <i>failing</i> the roll from an Act of Hubris to be closer in intended frequency to a vampire taking the kind of damage they need to spend an entire day healing (which they are incentivized to avoid) than it is to the Conditions that vampires get from succeeding or failing at a Detachment check (which fade without resolution after a number of nights and whose resolutions render their subject immune to the Condition for a month, when the game's diceless feeding mechanism prompts Detachment checks at a minimum threshold of right below a starting character's Humanity rating, one of the core clan Banes is built to make them gravitate towards desensitizing themselves to a comfortable Humanity rating Aloof from the living, and it has been pointed out that the frequent checks one is likely to make at high Humanity are fairly likely to succeed), not because three Mana is worth less than five Vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Horror hungers another take on Aspirations or something they have in addition to Aspirations that gets included in their rules in Hunter Second Edition? Although you're saying the blue book, but I can't find any description there of them having anything other than Aspirations (even if the animalistic ones might merely Aspire to satisfy certain appetites). Either way, I'm not really seeing the case for that being anything other than a psychological phenomenon in its own right. </div> </div> </div>They're Aspirations, and the ones related to feeding specifically produce Willpower that the Horror can retain outside the confines of the scene in which it is earned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with what I am inferring about the fact that some Deviants have multiple consciousnesses that come with separate Aspirations. </div> </div> </div>You infer incorrectly to the degree that there is a sidebar underlying the difference. The Symbiote form is &quot;your powers have an agenda, represented as one or more Aspirations, which can benefit or penalize attempts to use your Variations in support of or opposition to them&quot; as distinct from &quot;you have an Alternate Persona with its own Aspiration.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sure, Obsessions don't always represent conscious, deliberate goals and drives of a character, but they often do. Considering the elements described in those Conditions, I think the Obsessions they force of &quot;dominate others&quot; and &quot;use magic indiscriminately&quot; can be considered wilful rather than signalling the Storyteller to bring things into contact with them. </div> </div> </div>And I am purporting that this change is sufficiently adjacent to the deep subconscious to not be considered a phenomenon on the same level as &quot;someone messed with my memories&quot; or &quot;I have been made to feel despair,&quot; particularly given that I do not believe you are going to also suggest that Mystery Commands can be shrugged off in this manner since it involves Exarchal influence (despite the Exarchs not being wholly external forces due to the same cosmological placement of the Supernal that the Mastigos and Acanthus writeups allude to in their Stereotypes sections and one of the overarching problems of trying to reform the Enraptured).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are the impulses of Horrors and that subset of Deviants not the kind of thing that is subject to the Mind Arcanum? Are they off limits to Psychic Reprogramming? </div> </div> </div>Would you treat the Fate-based inclinations of the Principle and the God-Machine upon the world as psychological phenomena? Are you legitimately comparing Psychic Reprogramming to Pattern Restoration?<br /> <br /> They're Conditions modeling the consequences of losing the bit of your soul that keeps a lid on your magic's ability to ride your unconscious impulses and fine social-mystical connections due to carelessness or malice, rewriting an element of your character sheet that serves as a source of Mana and affecting your ability to regain or retain Willpower. These are deeper changes than being befuddled by a cryptid or addicted to vampire blood, and they come from the character themselves \u2014 if they had these Conditions or similar ones as a Sleeper and underwent the Awakening, I don't think it would be reasonable for them to be subject to the &quot;external supernatural effects are removed&quot; effect, so I would definitely not let them be removed by spending less than half the character's maximum Mana on Pattern Restoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T12:24:06-07:00","id":1517511,"title":"","content":"Just two notes. Improved pattern restoration only affects physical healing because it is an attainment of the Life Arcana, you could easily come up with an improved pattern restoration which is a Mind Arcana attainment and which makes the effects on Mental conditions better.<br /> <br /> The Time shielding effect also seems like it is way too powerful when it applies to &quot;conditions which worsen with time&quot; and you realise Soulless-ness worsens with time, so you could easily Shield it RAW.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517420#post1517420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Wards and Signs</u> makes no distinction between harmful and non-harmful, all shall be Withstood! Seriously though, unless one added a Key to it, Prime Shielding is fairly indiscriminate</div> </div> </div> </div>You are definitely the only person i have come across how interprets this in this manner.<br /> <br /> The phrase 'shields the subject from the effects of hostile magic' is usually used for justifying the opposite position.<br /> <br /> Of course you can Creative Thaumatergy a spells which acts the way you describe.<br /> <br /> And if the Imago contains a well defined* shielding effect (to only protect against certain types of effect) then the reverse interpretation should also be fine - as you describe a key, does keying a spell usually involve extra reach?<br /> <br /> *And by well defined, i mean a spell effect which is defined clearly at the time of casting/in the Imago, so it doesn't require the Archmaster practice of Dynamics... Spells can do different things depending on the circumstances, so long as those circumstances are static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-08-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T13:03:13-07:00","id":1517515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517511#post1517511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are definitely the only person i have come across how interprets this in this manner.<br /> <br /> The phrase 'shields the subject from the effects of hostile magic' is usually used for justifying the opposite position.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only say it's indiscriminate because of the phrasing of the second line (Emphasis mine):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the subject is the target of <u><b>a spell</b></u>, that spell is Withstood with the Potency of Wards and Signs. </div> </div> </div>Generally I assume the first line of a spell is the flavor/fluff, with the subsequent lines being primarily mechanics. Plus, <u>Ward</u> and other similar Shielding spells tend to be indiscriminate unless Keyed. It's more interesting (to me) to have to consciously build in exceptions to your defenses. That being said, thats just my interpretation and I could easily be wrong about the author's intent.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T14:12:28-07:00","id":1517518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517511#post1517511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Time shielding effect also seems like it is way too powerful when it applies to &quot;conditions which worsen with time&quot; and you realise Soulless-ness worsens with time, so you could easily Shield it RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! Soulless and Enervated get worse whenever you indulge your Vice, and Thrall is the endpoint of the continuum the other two Conditions represent once you've dropped to WIsdom/Integrity 1 and Willpower 0, but the time-based effects of soullessness are <i>recovering </i>from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T01:07:39-07:00","id":1517544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517515#post1517515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only say it's indiscriminate because of the phrasing of the second line (Emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally I assume the first line of a spell is the flavor/fluff, with the subsequent lines being primarily mechanics. Plus, <u>Ward</u> and other similar Shielding spells tend to be indiscriminate unless Keyed. It's more interesting (to me) to have to consciously build in exceptions to your defenses. That being said, thats just my interpretation and I could easily be wrong about the author's intent.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a perfectly fine interpretation, as a comparison:<br /> Every other shielding spell either provides a clash of Wills (which I presume a Mage can choose to fail without rolling) or only protects against damage (Alchemist's touch) or conditions/tilts (which i think for the environment are always negative).<br /> <br /> Veil of Moments explicitly does stop positive things (which get better with time) but allows reach options to exclude them.<br /> <br /> So i guess, in your interpretation, would you require a +1 reach option to add a key (as i think the rules for keying spells are underwritten).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T01:12:09-07:00","id":1517545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517518#post1517518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope! Soulless and Enervated get worse whenever you indulge your Vice, and Thrall is the endpoint of the continuum the other two Conditions represent once you've dropped to WIsdom/Integrity 1 and Willpower 0, but the time-based effects of soullessness are <i>recovering </i>from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would note, the reach option for Veil of Moments explicitly allows the subject to ignore Persistent Conditions. Which Soulless, Enervated and Thrall are - this may be an issue with the game design using conditions and tilts as it does, rather than being intentional, but i think RAW, Veil of Moments allows the Subject ignore Soul loss. (If they have lost all their Gnosis/Willpower they still can't cast spells, but if you catch it before it gets that bad, you could concievably using Mind magic to regain willpower... And take the reach option in veil of moments to heal normally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T05:11:42-07:00","id":1517556,"title":"","content":"I think while the intention is clear on things like that, Mage is loaded with mechanisms to get around those kinds of restrictions. Like you can't mess with a Vampire's Humanity or a Ghost's Synergy, but with some reach, WP, and Rewrite History you can indefinitely undo an Embrace or a Pact. I think the same mechanism could be used to revert soul loss, at least for the duration of the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T07:41:26-07:00","id":1517561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages?p=1517556#post1517556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think while the intention is clear on things like that, Mage is loaded with mechanisms to get around those kinds of restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for the purposes of discussing how the game is designed to work, I do not care what knots you can technically tie the system into to allow the game to produce an effect that doesn't work in-setting. If you aren't running a game where the idea is that the game mechanics are the root of the described fiction instead of the means used to arbitrate what happens, the design intention matters more for figuring out how to proceed than the technicalities of plugging one mechanic into another. The Peasant Railgun and the Locate City Nuke are funny mechanical exercises in older editions of Dungeons and Dragons, but nobody seriously recommends them in a game that isn't leaning into the screwball antics of &quot;let's break Dungeons and Dragons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T08:48:37-07:00","id":1517564,"title":"","content":"I think I actually agree very much with what you're saying, though I wonder how to reconcile, from a design intention standpoint, some things like this. Like on one hand it's clear that undoing an Embrace entirely (for the spell duration) is within the intended design space of mage, but not undoing the growth of blood potency. I resolve it by removing that Reach option because I'm not a good enough ST or designer to reconcile it another way, and I'm wondering what others do especially as it intersects that general kind of ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 07-09-2023, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T01:52:56-07:00","id":1521653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1/ Mages are Squishy: The most obvious point is that Mages are just ordinary people when you look at it and break easy. Sure they can get Mage armor, but some of the mage armors are tougher than others and using Mana to heal is very inefficient compared to other splats.</span></span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2/ Mages need to prepare: Mages are virtual demigods when they have time to prepare with rituals, but when caught unprepared they are vulnerable</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are as squishy as their long-term protective spells are, and this can be pretty un-squishy. Awakened etiquette (and that depends on ST view on it a lot) aside, not a lot of things prohibit you from casting a long-term protection spell or several of those on yourself and your cabalmates and shedding them on your Sleepwalker assistant or holding it yourself. Given, for example, 3 members of cabal with Gnosis 3 each, that gives 6 spellslots they can use to ward themselves and leave 1 free spellslot for everyday casting each. Cabal is a great force multiplier, also taking care of second problem...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3/ Mages have blind spots: My impression is that Mages can usually do some things really well, but are not that useful in others. For instance, a Mage with a high value in the Death Arcana would be great against Ghosts, but pretty hopeless when faced with a Spirit.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>...if you don't have Arcanum, you cabalmate possibly has it. In big (5+ mages) cabals it's pretty possible that every Arcanum is going to be had by at least one member of cabal, and if we are talking about grown-up mages (remember that starting characters are fresh-out-of-Order training mages), it's entirely possible cabal is going to have each of them at 3+. There is a <i>reason</i> why mages gather into cabals - they are <i>extremely</i> good force multipliers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4/ Mages need Mana: My impression is that Mana is mainly used to prevent paradox due to reach (correct me if I am wrong), and that Mages can burn through it quickly through spell casting. They also need it for Healing (however limited). However, if they burn through their Mana reserves they are forced to confront Paradox which might blow up in their faces, or scourge their bodies which is very unhealthy.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much true, especially if we are talking about older mages again. Important thing is that Paradox, especially if released, is not always a short-term problem for the Mage, but it always brings long-term problems: need to cover up incident, need to answer to other mages for the mess they caused, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515669-making-life-challenging-for-mages#post1515669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know if I am missing anything. </span></span>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>From my point of view and experience, the greatest weakness of mages is that they don't have any immediate apparent weaknesses and a lot of strengths. This creates a sense of false security and decreased risk management; mages often feel that they can solve <i>every</i> problem, but eventually <i>quantity</i> of problems becomes a <i>quality</i> of it's own. I gotta say, this is <b>not</b> a bane-like thing you can immediately use on every given mage and expect him to fold. There isn't a singular obvious weakness you can use to make Awakened life hard. But if you keep adding heat to the fire, they can and will make their own lives very hard.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}